  "research_note": "FIELD, LEITER & CO., built by T-3688 for the 1871 scene: the dry goods house of Marshall Field and Levi Z. Leiter, in Potter Palmer's marble building on the north-east corner of State and Washington Streets from the autumn of 1868 (Andreas vol. 2, pp. 563, 694-695). Built to Andreas's engraving of it. On the night of the fire its own pumps kept 'that massive pile of pure marble and iron' wet until the water failed (p. 734); it burned before daylight on 9 October 1871, with losses of nearly $3,500,000.",
